  "instructions": [
    {
      "text": "In a roasting pan, let the roast sit at room temperature for 60 minutes.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/perfect-sunday-roast/#wprm-recipe-50905-step-0-0",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/03/perfect-sunday-roast-01.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Preheat the oven to 375F. Mix the spices together in a small bowl.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/perfect-sunday-roast/#wprm-recipe-50905-step-0-1",
      "imageSource": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Rub the roast down with the seasonings, making sure the whole top is liberally covered.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/perfect-sunday-roast/#wprm-recipe-50905-step-0-2",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/03/perfect-sunday-roast-05.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Now, for the hard part. Let the roast sit in the oven for 1 hour. After 1 hour, turn off the oven completely. Let the roast sit in the oven for 3 hours. Do NOT open the oven door – you want the residual heat to continue cooking the meat. Remove the roast from the oven and cover with foil. Let it rest for 10 minutes additionally.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/perfect-sunday-roast/#wprm-recipe-50905-step-0-3",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/03/perfect-sunday-roast-06.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Slice the roast as thick as you’d like it. Serve! I had this with a side of broccoli with ranch and hot sauce.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/perfect-sunday-roast/#wprm-recipe-50905-step-0-4",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/03/perfect-sunday-roast-11.jpg"
    }
  ],
